1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,050
A sea route thousands of kilometres away
could make your online shopping more

2
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:04,880
expensive.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:08,510
This is the Red Sea, connected to the
Mediterranean through the Suez Canal.

4
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:12,220
It provides one of the shortest
shipping routes between Asia and Europe.

5
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:15,050
Now imagine ships could
no longer use this route.

6
00:00:15,190 --> 00:00:18,420
They might have to travel around the
Cape of Good Hope in southern Africa.

7
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:20,430
That's thousands of extra kilometres.

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,310
Longer journeys mean more fuel,

9
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:25,610
higher shipping costs and
possible delays in global trade.

10
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,800
A problem in one narrow region can
affect products all around the world.

11
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:32,400
Tomorrow, let's imagine
something even bigger:

12
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:35,120
what if English disappeared
from India overnight?

